WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.485 --> 00:00:03.577
- He's a businessman,
investor, and is involved in

00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:05.898
over 400 companies.

00:00:05.898 --> 00:00:08.706
He takes on big companies,
breaks the rules,

00:00:08.706 --> 00:00:11.172
and likes to go after world records.

00:00:11.172 --> 00:00:14.255
He's worth an estimated $4.9 billion.

00:00:15.212 --> 00:00:16.962
He's Richard Branson.

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:21.553
- And here are his top
10 rules for success.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.551
(swooshing)

00:00:26.551 --> 00:00:28.441
- I mean, I am dyslexic

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:30.863
and therefore I think I've been

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:34.161
very good at keeping things simple

00:00:34.161 --> 00:00:38.328
because, yeah, as a dyslexic
I need things to be simple

00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:43.170
for myself, and therefore Virgin, I think,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.883
when we launch a financial
service company or a bank

00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:49.304
we do not use jargon,
everything is very clear cut,

00:00:49.304 --> 00:00:53.836
very simple, and I think
people have an affinity

00:00:53.836 --> 00:00:57.334
to the Virgin brand because
we don't talk above them

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.841
or talk down to them.

00:00:58.841 --> 00:01:01.145
I mean, I think that lots of
people do not have the courage

00:01:01.145 --> 00:01:03.403
to try to start a business.

00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:05.211
And all I would say about it,

00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:07.129
I've written the book
called Screw It Just Do It,

00:01:07.129 --> 00:01:10.506
and it basically is
trying to say to people,

00:01:10.506 --> 00:01:11.730
just give it a try.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.881
Actually sometimes a very,
very small amount of money

00:01:13.881 --> 00:01:15.881
is all that's needed to start a company.

00:01:15.881 --> 00:01:18.845
My mother found a bracelet on the street

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.611
and she handed it in
to the police station,

00:01:20.611 --> 00:01:23.068
and after three months
the police let her sell it

00:01:23.068 --> 00:01:27.285
and the couple of hundred
dollars was really critical

00:01:27.285 --> 00:01:30.131
at a critical time in the
development of our business.

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:33.408
So all I say is just give it a go

00:01:33.408 --> 00:01:35.352
and good luck with that one.

00:01:35.352 --> 00:01:37.935
That I think the most important

00:01:40.012 --> 00:01:43.039
thing about running a company

00:01:43.039 --> 00:01:47.694
is to remember all the
time what a company is.

00:01:47.694 --> 00:01:50.649
A company is simply a group of people,

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:54.816
and as a leader of people you
have to be a great listener,

00:01:56.307 --> 00:01:58.654
you have to be a great motivator,

00:01:58.654 --> 00:02:02.060
you have to be very good at praising

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.769
and looking for the best in people.

00:02:04.769 --> 00:02:06.832
People are no different from flowers,

00:02:06.832 --> 00:02:08.904
if you water flowers they flourish,

00:02:08.904 --> 00:02:11.372
if you praise people they flourish,

00:02:11.372 --> 00:02:15.205
and that's the critical
attribute of a leader.

00:02:16.991 --> 00:02:19.341
You know, there is a very
thin dividing line between

00:02:19.341 --> 00:02:22.927
success and failure when you
start a business from scratch

00:02:22.927 --> 00:02:25.968
and if you don't have enough
money to pay the bills

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.815
you go the wrong side
of that dividing line,

00:02:27.815 --> 00:02:30.850
and if you can somehow get
enough money to pay the bills

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.872
you stay the right side
of that dividing line.

00:02:32.872 --> 00:02:35.655
You know, I've always been
running, either running faster

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:39.217
than perhaps I should, and
I have great difficulty

00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:42.094
saying no to things so I
keep on taking on new things,

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.425
and we've just managed
to stay the right side

00:02:44.425 --> 00:02:48.278
of the dividing line over the
last 50 years of business,

00:02:48.278 --> 00:02:50.935
but equally in those early days

00:02:50.935 --> 00:02:53.970
when you're starting a
business without any financial

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.849
backing, it's easy to slip the wrong side,

00:02:57.849 --> 00:03:01.468
and, in fact, most entrepreneurs
do slip the wrong side

00:03:01.468 --> 00:03:05.081
and the important thing is
then just pick yourself up

00:03:05.081 --> 00:03:09.583
and start again, and if it
doesn't work at that time

00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:13.014
then keep going until you do succeed,

00:03:13.014 --> 00:03:14.774
and not to give up.

00:03:14.774 --> 00:03:18.857
I think the next stage is
to be a great delegator

00:03:21.504 --> 00:03:23.332
and not try and do everything yourself.

00:03:23.332 --> 00:03:26.070
Try to find people who
are better than you,

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.265
all the time try to find
people who are better than you

00:03:28.265 --> 00:03:30.108
to put you out of business effectively,

00:03:30.108 --> 00:03:34.220
so whatever you are
spending all your day doing,

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:37.214
try to find someone who's
better than you to do that,

00:03:37.214 --> 00:03:40.376
to replace you at it,
so that you can go off

00:03:40.376 --> 00:03:44.128
and think about the next big picture.

00:03:44.128 --> 00:03:47.093
You know, an entrepreneur
is not a manager.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:50.932
An entrepreneur is
somebody who is great at

00:03:50.932 --> 00:03:55.015
conceiving ideas, starting
ideas, building ideas,

00:03:57.317 --> 00:03:59.458
but then handing over
to really good managers

00:03:59.458 --> 00:04:01.055
to manage the businesses.

00:04:01.055 --> 00:04:02.947
You know, the moment you've
got more than one business

00:04:02.947 --> 00:04:05.506
you can't be hands on doing everything.

00:04:05.506 --> 00:04:08.422
I don't actually think that the stereotype

00:04:08.422 --> 00:04:11.086
of a businessperson
treading away with people

00:04:11.086 --> 00:04:14.121
to get to the top,
generally speaking, works.

00:04:14.121 --> 00:04:16.788
I think if you treat people well

00:04:17.949 --> 00:04:20.532
people will come back for more.

00:04:21.545 --> 00:04:23.183
And it's a very small world.

00:04:23.183 --> 00:04:27.658
I actually think that
the best way of becoming

00:04:27.658 --> 00:04:32.214
a successful business leader
is dealing with people

00:04:32.214 --> 00:04:35.299
fairly and well, and I'd like to think

00:04:35.299 --> 00:04:37.876
that's how we run Virgin.

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:39.209
I love learning,

00:04:40.427 --> 00:04:44.510
I've never actually thought
I was starting a company

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.677
as such, I just saw situations
as I traveled in life

00:04:50.988 --> 00:04:53.385
where I felt I could improve on the way

00:04:53.385 --> 00:04:54.962
things that have been
done by other people.

00:04:54.962 --> 00:04:59.129
So, one of my favorite phrases
is screw it let's do it,

00:05:00.541 --> 00:05:03.171
and I've used that phrase a lot of times.

00:05:03.171 --> 00:05:06.627
And we just love going in and trying to

00:05:06.627 --> 00:05:08.996
shake up industries and doing it better

00:05:08.996 --> 00:05:10.389
than it's been done before.

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:14.365
Yeah, when we launched
Virgin Atlantic 30 years ago

00:05:14.365 --> 00:05:17.387
the New York Times did a
review, and they did some

00:05:17.387 --> 00:05:19.296
market research and they said,

00:05:19.296 --> 00:05:20.971
first of all, with a name like Virgin

00:05:20.971 --> 00:05:23.692
it's not going to go the whole way.

00:05:23.692 --> 00:05:27.046
(everyone laughing)

00:05:27.046 --> 00:05:30.417
But secondly, they did
market research where it said

00:05:30.417 --> 00:05:32.606
only seven percent of people would fly

00:05:32.606 --> 00:05:35.822
on a airline called Virgin,
and we put our hands up

00:05:35.822 --> 00:05:37.815
and said, seven percent
would be just fine,

00:05:37.815 --> 00:05:40.061
and so we carried on with it,

00:05:40.061 --> 00:05:42.240
but there were a lot of skeptics out there

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.031
and there always will be lots of skeptics

00:05:44.031 --> 00:05:46.068
when you want to start something new.

00:05:46.068 --> 00:05:48.573
Everybody will tell you
why it's a bad idea,

00:05:48.573 --> 00:05:51.456
why you shouldn't do it,
why you'll lose everything

00:05:51.456 --> 00:05:54.307
you've got, and in the end
you just got to at them

00:05:54.307 --> 00:05:56.709
and try to prove them
wrong, but good luck.

00:05:56.709 --> 00:05:58.876
I think the word business,

00:06:00.416 --> 00:06:04.220
it becomes a business, but
what you're doing is you're

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.220
painting a picture, you're trying to

00:06:09.246 --> 00:06:11.536
create something to make a difference

00:06:11.536 --> 00:06:14.550
in other people's lives,
you have a blank canvas

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:18.332
and you're filling in every
little bit of that canvas

00:06:18.332 --> 00:06:21.665
to get every single little detail right,

00:06:22.599 --> 00:06:26.432
and if that canvas sings
out at you at the end

00:06:27.652 --> 00:06:30.288
and it's a beautiful
picture, your business is

00:06:30.288 --> 00:06:31.875
going to be successful.

00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:34.918
If bits of the canvas are not quite right,

00:06:34.918 --> 00:06:36.404
your business may fail.

00:06:36.404 --> 00:06:38.686
So if you set out to change people's lives

00:06:38.686 --> 00:06:42.840
you've got to get every
single little detail right,

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.436
you got to make sure that
the people that you're

00:06:45.436 --> 00:06:49.603
working with 100% believe
in what you're trying to do

00:06:50.927 --> 00:06:54.957
and you got to make sure
that what you're trying to do

00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:58.074
is worthwhile spending your time on,

00:06:58.074 --> 00:07:01.430
and in the end of the day
you want to be sure that

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.994
the people's lives you've affected,

00:07:03.994 --> 00:07:06.080
you've really bettered
it, you've affected them

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.790
and benefited them, and
if you get all that right

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.156
hopefully you'll be able to pay the bills

00:07:12.156 --> 00:07:13.489
at the end of the year.

00:07:13.489 --> 00:07:16.068
- [Man] I would say the
overarching and key thing that

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.985
really binds the group
together is the idea of

00:07:19.985 --> 00:07:23.811
not just playing the game,
but changing it for good.

00:07:23.811 --> 00:07:26.669
I think Richard embodies
the principles better than

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:29.170
anyone I've ever worked
with and anybody that I know

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:32.279
because he's very focused on the business,

00:07:32.279 --> 00:07:34.541
on starting new businesses,

00:07:34.541 --> 00:07:37.550
on making sure that he's
got the right people

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:41.077
in the businesses, but also
on doing things differently

00:07:41.077 --> 00:07:43.591
and really changing the game.

00:07:43.591 --> 00:07:46.709
I think that it's the combination of those

00:07:46.709 --> 00:07:48.812
that sets him apart as
the great entrepreneur

00:07:48.812 --> 00:07:49.898
of his generation.

00:07:49.898 --> 00:07:51.872
- Thank you guys for
watching, I made this video

00:07:51.872 --> 00:07:54.538
because Arlene D. asked me to,

00:07:54.538 --> 00:07:56.339
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:07:56.339 --> 00:07:59.228
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below

00:07:59.228 --> 00:08:00.577
and I'll see what I can do.

00:08:00.577 --> 00:08:02.472
I'd also love to know
which of Richard Branson's

00:08:02.472 --> 00:08:05.141
top 10 rules you like the most.

00:08:05.141 --> 00:08:06.628
Leave it in the comments and I'm going to

00:08:06.628 --> 00:08:07.805
join in the discussion.

00:08:07.805 --> 00:08:10.992
Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:10.992 --> 00:08:12.776
- Continue to believe.

00:08:12.776 --> 00:08:15.625
- And we'll see you soon.

00:08:15.625 --> 00:08:17.708
(laughs)

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:20.804
(swooshing)

